Given N ≤ 20, find number of ways to reach a target sum using subset masks. Use bitset<1<<N> to store reachable sums and shift‑OR technique. Code provided below.
```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
int main(){
    int N, target; cin>>N>>target; vector<int>a(N); for(int&i:a)cin>>i;
    const int MAX = 1<<N; // up to 2^20 ≈ 1M bits
    bitset<1<<20> dp; dp[0]=1; // sum 0 reachable
    for(int x:a){
        dp |= (dp<<x); // shift left by x and OR
    }
    cout<<(dp[target]?"YES":"NO")<<"\n";
}
```
Explanation: `dp<<x` shifts all reachable sums by x, `|=` merges new sums. Complexity O(N*MAX/word_size).

